=================================================
1️⃣ System load (very important)
=================================================
load average: 0.02, 0.15, 0.23


These are 1 / 5 / 15 minute load averages.
All values << 1
Means CPU is mostly idle
No backlog of runnable processes
✅ System is NOT under load


Load average = average number of processes that are:
Runnable (using CPU or waiting for CPU)
OR uninterruptible (waiting for I/O like disk)

| State | Meaning                          | Counted? |
| ----- | -------------------------------- | -------- |
| `R`   | Running / ready to run           | ✅ Yes    |
| `D`   | Uninterruptible sleep (disk I/O) | ✅ Yes    |

------------------------------------
TO fetch these process id's
------------------------------------
ps -eo state,pid,cmd | grep '^D' 
ps -eo state,pid,cmd | grep '^R'

Add --> |wc -l --> to get the count of it
Formula:
new_load = old_load × e^(-5/τ) + current_load × (1 - e^(-5/τ))
Where:
τ = 1, 5, 15 minutes
current_load = number of runnable + uninterruptible processes


📌 Load must be compared to CPU cores

------------------------------------
IMP: Why high load with low CPU happens
------------------------------------
Very important real-world scenario:

CPU idle: 90%
Load avg: 10.0
Reason:
Many processes stuck in D state
Usually disk I/O or NFS/network storage issue
👉 Load ≠ CPU usage

=================================================
2️⃣ Tasks (process states)
=================================================
Tasks: 185 total, 1 running, 184 sleeping, 0 stopped, 0 zombie


1 running → normal
0 zombie → very healthy
Most processes are sleeping → idle system
✅ No process issues


| Code | Meaning    |
| ---- | ---------- |
| R    | Running    | Process is currently executing on CPU /
| S    | Sleeping   | Waiting for an event (I/O, signal, timer)
| D    | Disk sleep | Uninterruptible Sleep (I/O wait) / 
| T    | Stopped    | Process execution stopped
| Z    | Zombie     | Process has finished execution -> Parent has NOT collected exit status

D state is dangerous
=================================================
3️⃣ CPU breakdown
=================================================
%Cpu(s):  3.0 us,  2.0 sy, 94.3 id, 0.2 wa, 0.3 st


Meaning:
94.3% idle → CPU is free
3% user + 2% system → light workload
0.2% wa → almost no I/O wait
0.3% st (steal time) → negligible (good for VM)
✅ CPU is extremely healthy

🚨 Interview tip:
If st > 5–10%, it indicates noisy neighbor problem on cloud VMs.


